// Extra JVM coverage for issue #350's shape family: a self-recursive local
// `fun`, re-declared on every iteration of a `for` loop, with the loop
// inside a `try` block (V6_self_recursive_closure_in_loop.lox's own shape,
// wrapped in a try). Each iteration must still seed its own fresh
// self-capture cell (seedSelfCaptureCell, jvm_emitter.cpp) -- two closures
// from different iterations must stay distinct, not alias the same cell.
// Unlike the other examples in this group, this one does not actually
// need this PR's own fix: `f` is declared one block deeper than the try's
// own top-level scope (inside the loop body), so the catch clause's own
// `e` binding reuses a DIFFERENT, uncaptured slot, not `f`'s -- confirmed
// by running this file against the emitter with both #350/#388 fixes
// removed, which already prints `false` correctly. Kept anyway as
// coverage that self-recursion inside a loop inside a try/catch still
// verifies and runs correctly end to end.

var fns = [];
try {
    for (var i = 0; i < 3; i = i + 1) {
        fun f() { return f; }
        fns.append(f);
    }
} catch (e) { print e; }
print (fns[0] == fns[1]);

// CHECK: false
